1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,649
Reply lena aasaan hai.

2
00:00:02,869 --> 00:00:09,269
Lekin aisa reply lena jis par aapka
program bharosa kar sake, uske liye thodi care

3
00:00:09,269 --> 00:00:09,893
chahiye.

4
00:00:10,113 --> 00:00:15,806
Iss lesson mein aap reply ki length
control karoge, reply ko banate banate screen

5
00:00:15,806 --> 00:00:21,710
par dikhaoge, free text ki jagah
structured JSON loge, aur un cases ko handle karoge

6
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:23,959
jahan model jaldi ruk jaata hai.

7
00:00:25,259 --> 00:00:29,868
Aap max tokens use karoge, aur
har baar stop reason check karoge.

8
00:00:30,218 --> 00:00:34,094
Replies ko stream karoge,
taaki interface fast lage.

9
00:00:34,444 --> 00:00:37,914
Structured outputs se validated JSON loge.

10
00:00:38,264 --> 00:00:41,020
Aur refusals ko safely handle karoge.

11
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:44,965
Har response batata hai ki woh kyun ruka.

12
00:00:45,185 --> 00:00:47,006
Yeh field hai stop reason.

13
00:00:47,356 --> 00:00:52,019
End turn ka matlab: model ne
apna answer naturally poora kiya.

14
00:00:52,369 --> 00:00:57,910
Max tokens ka matlab: aapki limit aa
gayi aur reply beech mein kat gaya, shayad

15
00:00:57,910 --> 00:00:59,243
aadhe sentence par.

16
00:00:59,593 --> 00:01:04,586
Refusal ka matlab: model ne
safety reasons se request mana kar di.

17
00:01:04,936 --> 00:01:09,952
Stop sequence: model ne aapka diya
hua koi custom stop text likh diya.

18
00:01:10,302 --> 00:01:13,816
Tool use: model aapka
koi tool chalana chahta hai.

19
00:01:14,036 --> 00:01:17,009
Yeh agents ka dil hai, Module 5 mein.

20
00:01:17,359 --> 00:01:23,190
Aur pause turn: ek lamba agentic turn
ruka hai, aur aap usse continue kar sakte ho.

21
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:30,640
Max tokens ko exam ki word limit ki
tarah socho, ek strict invigilator ke saath.

22
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:35,429
Time khatam, aur invigilator paper
beech sentence mein hi le leta hai.

23
00:01:35,649 --> 00:01:39,697
Model apna answer limit
ke hisaab se plan nahi karta.

24
00:01:39,917 --> 00:01:42,007
Usse bas rok diya jaata hai.

25
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:45,464
Aur stop reason batata
hai ki aisa hua ya nahi.

26
00:01:46,764 --> 00:01:49,385
Hum ek hi question do baar puchte hain.

27
00:01:49,605 --> 00:01:54,396
Ek baar badi limit ke saath, ek
baar sirf pandrah tokens ke saath.

28
00:01:54,746 --> 00:01:57,244
Pehli run: hazaar tokens ki limit.

29
00:01:57,464 --> 00:02:00,968
Stop reason end turn,
matlab answer complete hai.

30
00:02:01,318 --> 00:02:03,472
Doosri run: pandrah tokens.

31
00:02:03,692 --> 00:02:08,410
Stop reason max tokens, aur
theek pandrah output tokens use hue.

32
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,561
Answer beech mein kat gaya.

33
00:02:10,911 --> 00:02:13,250
Aur yeh check sabse important hai.

34
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:16,975
Kata hua reply ek normal
string jaisa hi dikhta hai.

35
00:02:17,195 --> 00:02:22,957
Check nahi kiya, toh aap users ko aadha
answer dikha doge, ya aadhe JSON ko parse

36
00:02:22,957 --> 00:02:24,664
karne ki koshish karoge.

37
00:02:25,014 --> 00:02:28,142
Toh max tokens kaam
ke hisaab se kaafi rakho.

38
00:02:28,362 --> 00:02:34,190
Paise bachane ke liye bahut kam mat
rakho, kyunki kata hua answer usually ek retry

39
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,825
ka kharcha karwata hai.

40
00:02:37,125 --> 00:02:38,224
Ab streaming.

41
00:02:38,444 --> 00:02:40,885
Isse online video ki tarah socho.

42
00:02:41,105 --> 00:02:45,924
Bina streaming ke, aap poori movie
download karte ho, phir play karte ho.

43
00:02:46,144 --> 00:02:51,768
Streaming ke saath, video kuch seconds
mein chal padti hai, aur baaki hissa peeche

44
00:02:51,768 --> 00:02:53,003
se aata rehta hai.

45
00:02:53,223 --> 00:02:57,767
Total data utna hi hai, lekin
intezaar bahut achha lagta hai.

46
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:02,070
Yaad hai, model ek ek
token karke likhta hai.

47
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:07,725
Bina streaming ke, aapka program poore
reply ka intezaar karta hai, aur screen

48
00:03:07,725 --> 00:03:08,910
khaali rehti hai.

49
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:14,910
Streaming mein API pieces bhejti rehti
hai jaise jaise woh bante hain, toh text

50
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:17,199
lagbhag turant dikhne lagta hai.

51
00:03:17,419 --> 00:03:21,346
Total time same, lekin
experience kaafi fast lagta hai.

52
00:03:21,566 --> 00:03:26,245
Bahut lambe replies par streaming
request timeout se bhi bachata hai.

53
00:03:27,545 --> 00:03:33,440
Messages dot stream bilkul create jaise
hi arguments leta hai, aur with ke saath

54
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:36,240
context manager ki tarah use hota hai.

55
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:41,545
Text stream text ke chhote pieces
deta hai, jaise jaise woh aate hain.

56
00:03:41,765 --> 00:03:47,193
Hum har piece turant print karte hain,
flush equals True ke saath, taaki woh buffer

57
00:03:47,193 --> 00:03:48,174
mein ruke nahi.

58
00:03:48,524 --> 00:03:54,365
Aur stream khatam hone par get final
message poora message object deta hai, stop

59
00:03:54,365 --> 00:03:58,015
reason aur usage ke
saath, bilkul create ki tarah.

60
00:03:58,235 --> 00:04:02,416
Video mein pieces turant aa
gaye kyunki fake API local hai.

61
00:04:02,636 --> 00:04:05,563
Lekin code path real
streaming wala hi hai.

62
00:04:06,863 --> 00:04:08,535
Ab structured output.

63
00:04:08,755 --> 00:04:11,910
Ek letter aur ek
government form mein fark socho.

64
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:16,042
Letter mein kuch bhi, kisi
bhi order mein likha ja sakta hai.

65
00:04:16,262 --> 00:04:19,875
Form mein fixed boxes hote
hain: naam yahan, date wahan.

66
00:04:20,095 --> 00:04:23,145
Form ko program bina
guess kiye padh sakta hai.

67
00:04:23,365 --> 00:04:26,852
Structured outputs model
se ek form bharwaate hain.

68
00:04:28,152 --> 00:04:34,049
Agents ko baar baar machine readable
output chahiye: ek quiz, ek plan, ek tool

69
00:04:34,049 --> 00:04:34,729
decision.

70
00:04:34,949 --> 00:04:37,754
Prompt mein sirf JSON maangna fragile hai.

71
00:04:37,974 --> 00:04:41,919
Extra words, galat keys,
ya toota JSON aa sakta hai.

72
00:04:42,269 --> 00:04:45,035
Structured outputs isse fix karte hain.

73
00:04:45,255 --> 00:04:51,636
Aap ek JSON schema dete ho, aur API
reply ko uss schema ke valid JSON tak hi limit

74
00:04:51,636 --> 00:04:52,415
karti hai.

75
00:04:52,635 --> 00:04:58,727
Pydantic class doge, toh SDK schema bhi
banata hai aur reply ko Python object mein

76
00:04:58,727 --> 00:05:00,213
parse bhi karta hai.

77
00:05:01,513 --> 00:05:04,834
Pehle Pydantic classes
se shape describe karo.

78
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:10,549
Ek question mein text, chaar options,
sahi answer ka index, aur explanation.

79
00:05:10,769 --> 00:05:13,395
Ek quiz mein topic aur questions ki list.

80
00:05:13,615 --> 00:05:16,875
Pydantic par Module 3
mein poora lesson hai.

81
00:05:17,095 --> 00:05:19,986
Abhi inhe typed
dataclasses ki tarah padho.

82
00:05:20,336 --> 00:05:26,372
Yeh Field constraints kehte hain: exactly
chaar options, aur index zero se teen tak.

83
00:05:26,592 --> 00:05:32,406
API ka schema support limited hai, toh
SDK yeh limits field descriptions mein daal

84
00:05:32,406 --> 00:05:35,951
deta hai, aur reply aane
par khud check karta hai.

85
00:05:36,301 --> 00:05:41,717
Phir create ki jagah messages dot
parse call karo, output format mein class do.

86
00:05:42,067 --> 00:05:45,692
Parsed output ek real,
validated Quiz object hai.

87
00:05:45,912 --> 00:05:50,870
Right side dekho: type hai
Quiz, topic HTTP, aur do questions.

88
00:05:51,090 --> 00:05:55,343
Dictionaries mein khodne ki
jagah aap attributes use karte ho.

89
00:05:55,563 --> 00:05:59,272
Offline fake schema valid
placeholder questions deta hai.

90
00:05:59,492 --> 00:06:05,518
Agar reply schema mein fit na ho, toh
SDK validation error raise karta hai, kharab

91
00:06:05,518 --> 00:06:06,621
data nahi deta.

92
00:06:07,921 --> 00:06:09,894
Aakhri case: refusals.

93
00:06:10,114 --> 00:06:15,961
Agar stop reason refusal hai, toh model
ne safety reasons se mana kiya, aur content

94
00:06:15,961 --> 00:06:17,369
khaali ho sakta hai.

95
00:06:17,589 --> 00:06:21,181
Isliye text padhne se
pehle stop reason check karo.

96
00:06:21,401 --> 00:06:27,672
Current models par API ek declined
request ko automatically doosre model par chala

97
00:06:27,672 --> 00:06:28,436
sakti hai.

98
00:06:28,656 --> 00:06:30,947
Iss feature ko fallbacks kehte hain.

99
00:06:31,167 --> 00:06:35,802
Hamara project isse on karta
hai, lesson six mein code dekhoge.

100
00:06:37,102 --> 00:06:38,561
Interview corner.

101
00:06:38,781 --> 00:06:41,537
LLM response ko stream kyun karte hain?

102
00:06:43,887 --> 00:06:49,845
Answer: generation token by token hoti
hai, toh streaming text ko bante hue dikhati

103
00:06:49,845 --> 00:06:50,132
hai.

104
00:06:50,352 --> 00:06:55,789
User ko turant progress dikhta hai,
total time same rehta hai, aur bahut lambe

105
00:06:55,789 --> 00:06:57,949
replies timeout se bachte hain.

106
00:06:58,169 --> 00:07:02,084
Trap: yeh mat bolna ki
streaming se model fast ho jaata hai.

107
00:07:02,304 --> 00:07:05,696
Woh sirf intezaar ko
chhota mehsoos karwati hai.

108
00:07:06,046 --> 00:07:10,751
Doosra question: ek LLM se
reliable JSON kaise lete ho?

109
00:07:13,101 --> 00:07:15,614
Answer: structured outputs use karo.

110
00:07:15,834 --> 00:07:21,757
JSON schema ya Pydantic model do, taaki
reply usi shape mein aaye, object mein parse

111
00:07:21,757 --> 00:07:26,057
karo, aur phir bhi stop
reason aur business rules check karo.

112
00:07:26,277 --> 00:07:30,089
Trap: prompt mein JSON
maango aur regex se theek karo.

113
00:07:30,309 --> 00:07:33,596
Yeh pehle unusual
reply par toot jaata hai.

114
00:07:34,896 --> 00:07:36,153
Practice time.

115
00:07:36,503 --> 00:07:41,585
Pehla: do sabse common stop reasons
kaun se hain, aur dono ka matlab kya hai?

116
00:07:41,935 --> 00:07:46,353
Doosra: stream dot py mein flush
equals True hata do, toh kya hoga?

117
00:07:46,703 --> 00:07:51,984
Teesra: Quiz schema mein ek
difficulty field add karo, easy, medium, ya hard.

118
00:07:52,334 --> 00:07:56,973
Aur scenario: JSON parsing sirf
lambe replies par fail hoti hai.

119
00:07:57,193 --> 00:08:00,177
Pehle kya check karoge, aur fix kya hoga?

120
00:08:07,477 --> 00:08:08,405
Quick check.

121
00:08:08,625 --> 00:08:14,615
Aapka code reply ko JSON ki tarah parse
karta hai, aur lambe reply par fail ho jaata

122
00:08:14,615 --> 00:08:14,900
hai.

123
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,321
Sabse pehle kya check karoge?

124
00:08:23,021 --> 00:08:25,637
Ki stop reason max tokens hai ya nahi.

125
00:08:25,857 --> 00:08:29,481
Kata hua reply JSON ke
beech mein khatam hota hai.

126
00:08:30,781 --> 00:08:31,621
Recap.

127
00:08:31,841 --> 00:08:35,366
Stop reason batata hai ki
reply complete hai ya nahi.

128
00:08:35,586 --> 00:08:37,222
Hamesha check karo.

129
00:08:37,572 --> 00:08:40,302
Responsive output ke liye stream karo.

130
00:08:40,652 --> 00:08:46,105
Validated JSON ke liye messages
dot parse ke saath structured outputs.

131
00:08:46,455 --> 00:08:50,146
Aur content padhne se
pehle refusal handle karo.

132
00:08:50,496 --> 00:08:52,781
Agla lesson: production basics.

133
00:08:53,001 --> 00:08:57,140
Errors, rate limits, retries,
aur yeh sab kitne ka padta hai.
